# Deployment

## Production server

- **Host:** Hostinger (shared hosting, SSH access available)
- **Project root on prod:** `/home/u372714627/domains/zaninirenovations.ca/public_html`
  - This is the Laravel root (contains `artisan`, `app/`, `public/`, etc.).
  - Always `cd` here before running any `php artisan ...` command on prod.

## Laravel scheduler (automated emails)

The app uses **one system cron entry** that runs every minute; Laravel decides when each job actually fires:

```bash
* * * * * cd /home/u372714627/domains/zaninirenovations.ca/public_html && php artisan schedule:run >> /dev/null 2>&1
```

Configured tasks live in `app/Console/Kernel.php` (quote reminders, day-before commencement notice, etc.). Without this cron, scheduled commands never run on production.

## Common prod commands

After pushing changes to production, SSH in and run from the project root:

```bash
cd /home/u372714627/domains/zaninirenovations.ca/public_html

# Recompile Blade templates and clear app cache.
php artisan view:clear
php artisan cache:clear

# Only re-run these if the site uses cached config/views in prod.
php artisan config:cache
php artisan view:cache
```

## Asset cache busting

Static CSS/JS assets are referenced with a `?v={{ filemtime(...) }}` query string
(see `resources/views/site/layouts/public.blade.php` and
`resources/views/admin/layouts/app.blade.php`). The version updates automatically
whenever the file on disk changes, so browsers and CDNs always pick up new
deploys without a manual purge.
